Files: gpu_top.c gpu_top.h gpu_top_amd.c gpu_top_nvml.c gpu_top_gui.c gpu_top_gui.h gpu_top_int.h gpu_top_metrics.inc
Copyright: 2023 Umio Yasuno (amdgpu_top, libdrm_amdgpu_sys);
 2026 Eugene Flanagin <eflanagin@pm.me> (the C reimplementation)
License: MIT and GPL-2+
Comment: The Big Top's GPU view is a C reimplementation of amdgpu_top and the parts of
 libdrm_amdgpu_sys it uses (https://github.com/Umio-Yasuno/amdgpu_top, MIT); the gpu_metrics layout
 tables were generated from libdrm_amdgpu_sys's bindings of the kernel's kgd_pp_interface.h (MIT).
 SRS's own code in these files is GPL-2+.

Files: ir.c
Copyright: 2024 Přemysl Eric Janouch <p@janouch.name> (elksmart-comm);
 2026 Eugene Flanagin <eflanagin@pm.me>
License: 0BSD and MIT and GPL-2+
Comment: The ELK Smart dongle protocol is a port of elksmart-comm.c from usb-drivers
 (https://git.janouch.name/p/usb-drivers, 0BSD; the notice is kept in the file header). The codes file,
 wording and udev rule follow IR Remote (https://github.com/eugenesflanagin-spec/irremote, MIT).
 SRS's own code is GPL-2+.

Files: data/power-zip-rates.tsv
Copyright: National Renewable Energy Laboratory (NREL), U.S. Electric Utility Companies and Rates:
 Look-up by Zip Code (2024), from U.S. EIA Form EIA-861 data; reformatted by SRS
License: CC-BY-4.0
Comment: Source: https://catalog.data.gov/dataset/u-s-electric-utility-companies-and-rates-look-up-by-zip-code-2024

Files: power_rates_data.inc
Copyright: U.S. Energy Information Administration (U.S. state average prices);
 Eurostat (European household prices); Ofgem (Great Britain price cap figures);
 Ember (grid CO2 intensity) - figures as published, with the code around them by Eugene Flanagin
License: public-domain and Eurostat-reuse and Ofgem-published and CC-BY-4.0 and GPL-2+
Comment: Each figure comes from one source: the U.S. prices from EIA (public domain), the European
 prices from Eurostat, the GB price cap from Ofgem, the CO2 intensities from Ember (CC BY 4.0). The
 sources and dates are listed at the top of the file, in CREDITS.md and in the user guide,
 "Power & Cost". The C code itself is GPL-2+.

License: public-domain
 Data of the U.S. Energy Information Administration are a work of the U.S. government and are in
 the public domain. Source credited as EIA asks.

